content:
{
  "asset": "Pump P-105, AquaDyne HF-300 end-suction centrifugal pump, serial HF3-22000, on the chemically dosed filtered-water line.",
  "priority": "P2",
  "stop_equipment_now": false,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Vibration: the applicable limit is HF-300 Figure 3, vibration velocity in mm/s RMS measured on bearing housings. The reported 3.9 mm/s is above the 2.8 mm/s Zone A/B boundary and below the 4.5 mm/s Zone B/C boundary, so it is Zone B, 'Long-term operation'. It is not in Zone C ('Restricted - plan maintenance') or the highest severity Zone D, so the reading does not trigger the SSP-07 immediate-stop rule.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Drive-end bearing housing temperature: the manual's housing-surface limits apply—normal up to 70 C, alarm at 80 C and trip at 90 C. The reported 71 C is 1 C above the normal maximum but remains 9 C below alarm and 19 C below trip. Because SSP-07 requires a priority-1 work order only when temperature is above the manufacturer's alarm limit, 71 C does not trigger that P1 rule; investigate the elevated temperature during the repair.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C09",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Shaft-seal leakage matches the manual symptom 'Leakage at shaft seal', for which the corrective action is mechanical-seal replacement and an alignment check. No numerical allowable leakage rate is supplied.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Immediate stop is not required by the reported values: vibration is Zone B and temperature is below the 90 C trip. The supplied documents do not define seal leakage alone as an immediate-stop criterion. The pump must nevertheless never be run dry.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "Worn or cracked mechanical-seal faces, potentially the bulletin-described early HF3-450 failure, are the leading hypothesis. If HF3-450 is installed, this pump is specifically within the affected population: field failures from serial HF3-22000 were attributed to a revised sleeve tolerance.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C09",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Shaft misalignment is a common possible contributor because it is listed as a cause of shaft-seal leakage, high vibration and high bearing temperature.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Seal dry running remains possible; the pump uses Plan 11 flush from pump discharge and the manual explicitly prohibits dry running.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Bearing wear or over-greasing, impeller imbalance or damage, and cavitation/inadequate NPSH remain diagnostic possibilities for the vibration and elevated temperature; the reported readings alone do not distinguish among them.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Before disassembly, complete the condition record: measure vibration velocity on both bearing housings and classify the highest reading with Figure 3; record bearing temperatures on the housing surfaces and compare them with the 70/80/90 C normal/alarm/trip limits.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C06",
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Isolate and drain the pump. Apply electrical isolation and LOTO at the MCC, mechanically isolate the suction and discharge valves, and obtain the line-break permit after draining and venting. Use the required chemical PPE throughout the seal work.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C15",
        "C16"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before lifting, obtain the shift supervisor's signed lifting plan and use certified lifting equipment: the back pull-out assembly weighs 68 kg, exceeding the 25 kg SSP-07 threshold. Remove the back pull-out assembly; its design permits removal without disturbing the casing or pipework.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C10",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Remove the impeller nut and impeller, then withdraw the existing seal and sleeve. Inspect the sleeve for scoring and measure scoring depth for the condition decision; replace sleeve HF3-455 if scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Investigate the associated symptoms: check shaft alignment, bearing grease quantity and NPSH; inspect both bearings and the impeller. If bearing replacement is required by the inspection/procedure, replace drive-end HF3-512 and non-drive-end HF3-510 together as a pair rather than replacing only one bearing.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before reassembly, obtain the manual Table 5 values for fasteners other than the seal gland nuts; do not extrapolate the cartridge-seal gland torque to other fasteners.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Fit one new pre-set cartridge seal HF3-450B and one new casing gasket HF3-120. Do not fit HF3-450 on this serial-numbered pump. No sleeve measurement is needed to set the pre-set cartridge seal. Tighten the HF3-450B seal gland nuts to 30 Nm; tighten other fasteners to their applicable Table 5 values.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Perform laser shaft alignment after any work that moves the motor or bearing housing, and as part of the leakage/vibration investigation. Acceptable tolerances are parallel offset 0.05 mm and angular misalignment 0.05 mm per 100 mm.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before operating the pump, establish the Plan 11 seal flush from pump discharge and ensure the seal is never run dry.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "On return to service, check the repaired seal and repeat vibration measurements on both bearing housings and housing-surface temperature checks. Classify the highest vibration using Figure 3. If vibration reaches the manufacturer's highest severity zone, stop immediately and notify the reliability engineer before restart; if bearing temperature exceeds the 80 C alarm limit, raise a P1 work order within the shift.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "C09",
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-450B",
      "description": "Pre-set cartridge mechanical seal; mandatory replacement for HF3-450 on this pump because serial HF3-22000 is included in SB-2026-014. Quantity one.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-120",
      "description": "Casing gasket; fit new with the seal replacement and whenever the casing is opened.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-455",
      "description": "Shaft sleeve; conditional replacement part, required if inspection finds scoring deeper than 0.1 mm.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-512",
      "description": "Drive-end bearing 6312-C3; conditional only if bearing-pair replacement is required. Replace together with HF3-510.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-510",
      "description": "Non-drive-end bearing 6310-C3; conditional only if bearing-pair replacement is required. Replace together with HF3-512.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "For work inside the pump or on its seal, use electrical isolation and LOTO at the MCC, mechanical isolation of both suction and discharge valves, and a line-break permit with draining and venting completed first.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Wear chemical goggles and nitrile gloves: P-105 falls within P-101 to P-106 on the filtered-water line, which is dosed with sodium hypochlorite.",
      "citations": [
        "C15",
        "C16"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "For the 68 kg back pull-out assembly, use a lifting plan signed by the shift supervisor and certified lifting equipment because the load exceeds 25 kg.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Maintain Plan 11 seal flush from pump discharge and never run the seal dry.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If subsequent vibration classification reaches the manufacturer's highest severity zone, stop the machine immediately and notify the reliability engineer before restart. The currently reported 3.9 mm/s Zone B reading does not activate this control.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "Mechanical seal replacement: standard allowance 4.0 hours with 2 technicians.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Laser alignment: standard allowance 1.5 hours with 1 technician; include it for the alignment check and whenever the motor or bearing housing is moved.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10",
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Conditional bearing-pair replacement: add the standard allowance of 6.0 hours with 2 technicians only if the inspection/procedure requires both bearings to be replaced.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10",
        "C12"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "Seal part conflict: the manual parts list identifies HF3-450, but SB-2026-014, issued 14 March 2026, says not to fit HF3-450 on HF-300 pumps serial HF3-22000 and above and to use HF3-450B instead. P-105 is exactly serial HF3-22000, so it is inside the inclusive bulletin range; HF3-450B governs for this asset.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Torque conflict: the general seal procedure directs fasteners to manual Table 5, whereas the bulletin specifies a 30 Nm gland-nut torque for HF3-450B, identifying 25 Nm as the former value. Because the bulletin and cartridge seal apply to this exact serial, use 30 Nm for the seal gland nuts; do not use the superseded 25 Nm value. Table 5 remains applicable to other fasteners, but its values were not supplied.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Sleeve-measurement scope: the bulletin's statement that no sleeve measurement is needed applies to setting the pre-set HF3-450B cartridge. It does not eliminate sleeve condition inspection, because the manual requires scoring inspection and the same bulletin requires sleeve replacement when scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "Which seal is currently installed, HF3-450 or HF3-450B, and is there any history of Plan 11 flush loss or dry running? This is needed to test the bulletin-related and dry-run hypotheses (C02, C09, C13).",
    "Does the reported 3.9 mm/s represent RMS velocity on a bearing housing, at which housing was it measured, and what is the other housing's reading? The manual requires both housings to be measured and the highest reading classified (C06, C07).",
    "What is the measured shaft-sleeve scoring depth, and is conditional sleeve HF3-455 therefore required? The replacement threshold is scoring deeper than 0.1 mm (C10, C13).",
    "What are the alignment readings, grease quantity, bearing noise/wear findings, impeller condition and NPSH/cavitation findings? These determine whether the conditional bearing-pair work and parts are required; no grease-quantity or NPSH acceptance criteria are supplied (C09, C10).",
    "What are the complete manual Table 5 torque values for the impeller nut and other non-gland fasteners? Only the 30 Nm HF3-450B gland torque is available in the evidence (C10, C13).",
    "What site priority matrix distinguishes P2 from P3, and what completion date is required? P2 is the planning selection for this non-emergency corrective repair, but the supplied site document explicitly defines only the P1 response for temperature above the 80 C alarm (C02, C15).",
    "Is there a site numerical limit for seal leakage or a specified post-repair leakage acceptance test? The supplied manual identifies leakage and its corrective action but provides no numerical leakage limit (C09)."
  ]
}
